WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.590
On Page 1, we located the loan terms and the estimated cash to close.

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:13.086
Page 2 answers the next question every borrower asks: where does that
money actually go?

00:00:13.086 --> 00:00:17.973
In this lesson, we are going to locate five areas of the closing cost

00:00:17.973 --> 00:00:23.907
detail — and find one section that most borrowers
never realize is an invitation.

00:00:23.907 --> 00:00:27.198
This is Page 2, the Closing Cost Details.

00:00:27.398 --> 00:00:30.608
It is organized into two columns.

00:00:30.808 --> 00:00:37.605
The left column shows Loan Costs — what the borrower pays in
connection with getting the loan itself.

00:00:37.605 --> 00:00:44.625
The right column shows Other Costs — items like
taxes, prepaids, and initial escrow.

00:00:44.625 --> 00:00:48.480
Both columns flow into one total at the bottom.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.780
First, locate Section A, Origination Charges.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.904
These are amounts charged by the lender for making the loan —

00:00:55.904 --> 00:01:01.368
and this is where discount points appear, when the
borrower is paying points.

00:01:01.368 --> 00:01:07.542
If a borrower asks what the lender itself is
charging, Section A is where you look.

00:01:07.542 --> 00:01:10.969
Next is Section B, Services You Cannot Shop For.

00:01:10.969 --> 00:01:15.938
These are services the lender requires and selects the provider for —

00:01:16.138 --> 00:01:18.623
items such as the appraisal.

00:01:18.823 --> 00:01:23.369
The borrower pays for them, but does not choose who performs them.

00:01:23.369 --> 00:01:27.003
Now look carefully at Section C, Services You Can Shop For.

00:01:27.003 --> 00:01:32.713
The estimate lists providers here, but the borrower is permitted to
choose different ones.

00:01:32.713 --> 00:01:37.754
This section is an invitation, not a list of decisions that have
already been made —

00:01:37.754 --> 00:01:45.916
and it is the section borrowers most often ignore, because nobody
explains that shopping is actually allowed.

00:01:45.916 --> 00:01:50.400
Both columns come together in Section J, Total Closing Costs.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.987
Notice the line for Lender Credits —

00:01:52.987 --> 00:01:58.824
amounts the lender contributes toward the borrower's costs, which
reduce the total.

00:01:58.824 --> 00:02:05.854
A borrower comparing two estimates should always compare Section J,
not a single line item.

00:02:05.854 --> 00:02:09.627
Finally, locate the Calculating Cash to Close table.

00:02:09.627 --> 00:02:13.654
It starts with total closing costs and walks line by line —

00:02:13.654 --> 00:02:20.968
the down payment, deposits already paid, and any credits — to the
estimated cash to close.

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:26.409
This is the arithmetic behind the single number the
borrower saw on Page 1.

00:02:26.409 --> 00:02:32.587
Here is the professional habit for Page 2: read it
by sections, not by lines.

00:02:32.587 --> 00:02:35.627
Section A is what the lender charges.

00:02:35.627 --> 00:02:40.186
Sections B and C are services — and Section C belongs to the borrower.

00:02:40.186 --> 00:02:48.675
A professional who never mentions that the borrower may shop has left
money on the table that was never theirs to leave.
